{"title":"2023 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> has three chords of equal length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a3346b4734de640197c09d1a4682f062d0009212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 2 \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" /> which intersect forming a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61ad11cc93b5c9730a1dc83da23b998ba98c7f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. The square of the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf558bbd380f9ed3c749db2269e17e9467653a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> squarefree. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72cde2a1ad8eacf550776cbdd7e6f7deb8f97070.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); pair A = (0,1); pair B = (-sqrt(3),0); pair C = (sqrt(3),0); pair O = (0,2*sqrt(3)-3);  draw((-2-sqrt(3),0)--(2+sqrt(3),0), red+linewidth(1)); draw((-3,1+sqrt(3))--(2*sqrt(3),-1), red+linewidth(1)); draw((3,1+sqrt(3))--(-2*sqrt(3),-1), red+linewidth(1)); draw(circle((0,2*sqrt(3)-3), sqrt(28-8*sqrt(3))), blue+linewidth(1.2)); draw(circle((0,2*sqrt(3)-3), 2*sqrt(3)-3), dotted+linewidth(0.8)); draw(A--B--C--cycle, black+linewidth(1.5)); draw(O--(2+sqrt(3),0),dotted+linewidth(1.2)); draw(O--(0,0),dotted+linewidth(1.2)); draw(O--(0,0),dotted+linewidth(1.2));  dot(A); dot(B); dot(C);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SW); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, N); [/asy]\" width=\"358\" height=\"358\" /> </center><p> Let the triangle formed from the intersection be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and the center of the circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since the three chords are of equal length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must be equidistant to sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The inradius is equal to the quotient of the area and semiperimeter, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242691a23d3b9f92760fe048eacf5742ffed9076.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\frac{2+2+2\\sqrt{3}}{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}} = 2\\sqrt{3}-3.\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"50\" /> From the Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8ce8ed1cac484fe0b0eb3eac8ce79860c70dc06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 = (2\\sqrt{3}-3)^2+(2+\\sqrt{3})^2 = (21-12\\sqrt{3})+(7+4\\sqrt{3})=28-8\\sqrt{3}\\implies28+8+3=\\boxed{39}.\\]\" width=\"660\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4679/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31920:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024444 and revision id 274650. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}